    "intro_html":  "One pot means one pot. The pasta cooks directly in the salsa and broth, which means the starch that normally goes down the drain stays in the pan and thickens the sauce for free. No colander, no second pot, no separate sauce. Each serving runs {{cal}} calories with \u003cstrong\u003e{{protein}} grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e for about \u003cstrong\u003e${{cost_ps}}\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost). Jarred salsa doing the job of six separate ingredients is one of the better shortcuts in a budget kitchen.",
